{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-bring-embeddable-knots-table-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:bring-embeddable-knots-table-data","kind":"table","title":"Bring-embeddable knot/link table by Seifert genus ($g = 0$ to $4$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-bring-embeddable-knots"],"tags":["bring-surface","knot-table","genus-bound","braid-word"],"text":"bring-embeddable-knots-table-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:bring-embeddable-knots-table-data\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g</code></th>\n<th>Canonical knots / links</th>\n<th>Braid word</th>\n<th>Vol (depth-2 period)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>unknot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0_1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{1}_{B_1}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>trefoil <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3_1 = T(2,3)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^3 \\in B_2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> (chiral, not hyperbolic)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>figure-8 <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4_1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2^{-1})^2 \\in B_3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2\\,\\mathrm{Cl}_2(\\pi/3) \\approx 2.02988</code> ✓</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5_2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^2 \\sigma_2^{-1} \\sigma_1 \\sigma_2^{-1} \\in B_3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 2.82812\\ldots</code> (chiral hyperbolic)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>proton <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}_3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2^{-1})^3 \\in B_3</code></td>\n<td>per the paper's recursive atom-knot atlas (<code>../appendix-knot-periodic-table/recursive-atom-knot-atlas.md</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6_2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6_3</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ldots</code></td>\n<td>various <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\in B_3, B_4</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 4.40083, 5.69301, \\ldots</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Borromean rings <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_{6a4}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2^{-1})^3 \\in B_3</code> closure</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8 G \\approx 7.32772</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(3, 4) = 8_{19}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2)^4 \\in B_3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> (torus, not hyperbolic)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>knots <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8_*</code> hyperbolic</td>\n<td>various</td>\n<td>various</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2, 9) = 9_*</code> torus</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1^9 \\in B_2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(3, 5) = 10_{124}</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\sigma_1 \\sigma_2)^5 \\in B_3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/bring-embeddable-knots-table-data.md","heading":"Table"}
